                <h2>Pre-Setup: Build a Reconciliation Ledger</h2>
<p>Before starting, create an "Ad Account Reconciliation Ledger" in Excel or an online spreadsheet with the following fields:</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Field</th>
<th>Description</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Account ID</td>
<td>Unique identifier from the platform</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Account Name</td>
<td>Easy-to-identify alias</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Platform</td>
<td>Meta / TikTok / Google</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Recharge Date</td>
<td>Actual recharge date</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Recharge Amount (USD)</td>
<td>Original recharge amount</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Recharge Amount (CNY)</td>
<td>Actual RMB expenditure</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Corresponding Spend (USD)</td>
<td>Actual spend in the reconciliation period</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Invoice Status</td>
<td>Received / Not Received / Under Review</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Notes</td>
<td>Difference explanation or special handling</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<hr />
<h2>Step 1: Verify Recharge Records</h2>
<p>Recharge is the starting point of cash flow—ensure every transaction is traceable.</p>
<h3>Steps</h3>
<ol>
<li>Log into the agency backend or ad platform and export this month's recharge records</li>
<li>Cross-check agency invoices, bank statements, and platform records for consistency</li>
<li>Confirm whether the recharge arrival time matches the spend start time (some platforms have processing delays)</li>
<li>Record the exchange rate (if settled in non-USD) to avoid calculation discrepancies</li>
</ol>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Common Issue</strong>: A utility app team reported that recharges made at month-end were consumed in the following month, causing a mismatch. Solution: Mark "Prepaid" and "Consumed" separately in the ledger.</p>
</blockquote>
<hr />
<h2>Step 2: Verify Spend Data</h2>
<p>Spend data is the core metric of advertising and the key element of reconciliation.</p>
<h3>Key Verification Points</h3>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Verification Dimension</th>
<th>Action</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Platform backend data</td>
<td>Download spend reports directly from the ad platform</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Agency backend data</td>
<td>Verify account balance and spend details shown in the backend</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Spend date range</td>
<td>Confirm complete data within the reconciliation period</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Currency consistency</td>
<td>Convert to USD or CNY uniformly for aggregation</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<h3>Difference Investigation</h3>
<p>If platform data doesn't match agency data, first check:<br />
- Any unapplied refunds or Credits<br />
- Frozen balance or unreleased pre-authorizations<br />
- Timezone settings causing data cutoff differences (recommend using UTC consistently)</p>
<hr />
<h2>Step 3: Invoice Receipt and Verification</h2>
<p>Invoices are essential for financial compliance, but overseas ad platforms have notably different invoice processes than domestic platforms.</p>
<h3>Invoice Retrieval by Platform</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Meta Business Manager</strong>: Download invoices under "Billing" → "Payment Settings." Note: Some accounts require business verification before receiving official invoices.</li>
<li><strong>TikTok Ads</strong>: Apply through your account manager or agency. Invoice types can be Invoice or Receipt.</li>
<li><strong>Google Ads</strong>: Log into the Google Ads backend and download statements and invoices under "Billing" → "Transactions."</li>
</ul>
<h3>Invoice Verification Checklist</h3>
<ul>
<li>[ ] Invoice amount matches recharge amount</li>
<li>[ ] Invoice recipient matches company entity</li>
<li>[ ] Invoice date falls within reconciliation period</li>
<li>[ ] Invoice number corresponds to recharge record</li>
<li>[ ] Invoice currency matches contract agreement</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2>Step 4: Difference Handling and Closure Confirmation</h2>
<h3>Common Difference Types</h3>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Difference Type</th>
<th>Possible Cause</th>
<th>Handling</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Recharge &gt; Spend + Balance</td>
<td>Some funds not yet consumed</td>
<td>Confirm as account balance, track next month</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Spend &gt; Recharge</td>
<td>Credits or prior month balance applied</td>
<td>Verify Credits source</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Invoice amount mismatch</td>
<td>Exchange rate difference or platform service fee</td>
<td>Confirm with agency and adjust</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<h3>Closure Confirmation</h3>
<p>After completing the above steps, mark the account status as "Verified" in the ledger and have the finance manager review and sign off (electronic signature accepted). Aim to complete reconciliation by the 10th of each month to avoid impacting monthly settlement.</p>
<hr />
<h2>Quick Checklist</h2>
<ul>
<li>[ ] Recharge records match agency invoices and bank statements</li>
<li>[ ] Spend data matches platform backend data</li>
<li>[ ] Invoices received and amounts verified</li>
<li>[ ] Difference items investigated and documented</li>
<li>[ ] Ledger updated and reviewed</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2>Summary</h2>
<p>Reconciling overseas ad accounts is more complex than domestic platforms, mainly due to multi-platform data aggregation, cross-currency conversion, and longer invoice processing cycles. Teams should fix reconciliation deadlines (e.g., 5th–10th of each month) and designate someone to follow up on discrepancies to prevent issues from accumulating. For teams managing multiple accounts, consider using automation tools with API integration for automatic data pulling and comparison.</p>
